from pathlib import Path
import re
root=Path.cwd()
p=root/'design.md';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
old_fw=next(line for line in s.splitlines() if '**Firmware/link:**' in line)
old_stall=re.search(r'The tidy stalled before its first look under `clock:=wall`.*?\(unexplained\)\.',s).group(0)
with (root/'design full history.md').open('a',encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write('\n\n## Nov 3, 2026 — statements superseded by the PC stack regression\n\n')
    f.write('From design.md 2.1 (protocol version correction; the existing fault-stop decision already specified v5):\n\n'+old_fw+'\n\n')
    f.write('From design.md 4.10 (previous wall-clock tidy observation, preserved; the stall did not recur in this regression):\n\n'+old_stall+'\n')
s=s.replace('COBS/CRC USB protocol 4,','COBS/CRC USB protocol 5,')
s=s.replace(old_stall,'The first-look wall-clock stall did not recur in the Nov 3 PC regression: Python/D435 navigate-then-tidy finished with 6/6 toys binned (4.5). The harness now has a configurable 600 s wall budget; its former 240 s limit had prematurely stopped another run at 2/6.')
s=s.replace('### 4.6 Localization, ROS and timing', '**PC stack regression, Nov 3 (sim, current ARM, seed 0, six toys, full Nav2/SLAM):** navigate-then-tidy finished with 6/6 physically binned and zero failed picks under both Python/D435/wall clock and C++ driver/stereo/sim clock. These are different conditions, not a camera or speed comparison. Simulation ran below real time; no Pi, real sensors or CAD validation. Raw D435 depth was retained: a single median-filter probe scored 5/6 versus raw 6/6, despite reporting six picks. Details and qualifications: [PC regression](simulation/v11%20sil/studies/results/pc_stack_2026-11-03.md).\n\n### 4.6 Localization, ROS and timing')
s=s.replace('### 4.7 Drive, supply and printing', '**PC regression, Nov 3:** current ARM/Python/D435/wall clock reached 8/8 house goals (0.113 m mean true arrival error). SLAM restart now rejects cached/old map transforms and recovers an inactive lifecycle node; console takeover targets launch descendants instead of a broad stop that could kill itself. Three map switches with explicit return-map initial poses were followed by a goal 0.052 m from truth. Loading a map still assumes its start unless the operator supplies a pose. The installed composed Nav2 can crash or require forced termination during shutdown; this remains open, separate from completed driving/picking results. See the PC regression report.\n\n### 4.7 Drive, supply and printing')
s += '\n| Nov 3 | PC stack regression: 8/8 house goals and 6/6 toys in both tested arm configurations; stale-TF/inactive-SLAM recovery and targeted console takeover fixed. Extend the tidy harness budget and score physical bin truth. Nav2 container shutdown remains an open vendor-level limitation (4.5–4.6). |\n'
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8')
r=root/'ros/README.md';text=r.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('protocol version (4)','protocol version (5)')
text += '\n\n## PC regression checks\n\nThe [Nov 3 desktop stack regression](../simulation/v11%20sil/studies/results/pc_stack_2026-11-03.md) covers manual driving and goals, SLAM/map switching, exploration, patrol, arm poses, navigate-then-tidy and injected stops. It records both successes and the remaining Nav2 container shutdown issue.\n\nUse `tools/console_smoke.py --slam --tabs --faults` against the supervisor\'s `robot` step with `person:=true`. It resets an already-enabled simulated person for Follow and supplies the return-map initial pose after Explore. For repeatable automation, pass `OMNI_FACE_ARGS="--mute --listen none"` when launching, so microphone input cannot steer a scripted test.\n\nFor the arm, pass camera, implementation and clock options directly to `omni.sh arm`, then run `tools/arm_load.py <out.json> --phases NAVTIDY,ROUTE --legs 1 --laps 1 --tidy-timeout 600` in the same ROS domain. The timeout is wall time: a 240 s budget can cut off a six-object tidy when the simulator runs below real time. Reports distinguish a started task, timeout, task pick count and physical bin count; picking is skipped after failed navigation.\n'
r.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')